## Hints

- E1: skew/kurt formulas assume normality AND independence; real r has
  fat tails + clustering — expect the simulated SEs of skew/kurt to be
  LARGER than the formulas.
- E2: SE(p1) shrinking like 1/√n; the target n is big — that's the
